  "query_preview": "period of moderate rainfall. Some locations will just \nsee light rain, but the higher end of the probabilistic envelope\nis impressive with an exceedance of 1 to 2 inches possible, \nespecially in the aforementioned north- northeast of Tucson \nareas and the higher terrain. This includes the Mogollon Rim \ninto the Gila National Forest, therefore increased flows in \ncreeks and rivers across northern Graham and Greenlee may be a \nconcern, including the San Francisco, Blue, and Gila rivers. The\nNBM shows a 40-70 percent chance of at least an inch Sunday \ninto Monday in these favored areas with 10-30 percent chances of\nat least 2 inches of rain.\n\nTemperatures across southeastern Arizona will fall with this\nweather maker duo, likely becoming coolest Sunday and \npotentially Monday. Currently forecast highs for Sunday are 7 to\nnear 15 degrees below normal and areas that see extensive cloud\ncover and rain through the day will likely be on the colder end\nof this spectrum.\n\nThough the main upper level wave will likely have exited to the\neast by Monday, lingering moisture and cyclonic flow aloft will\nkeep a chance of showers in the forecast.",
